    "module_designation": null,
    "description": "Family of indicating device / weighing module designated the WTM Series, designed to be used as part of a single-interval, Class III or IIII, non-automatic weighing instrument. The family comprises the WTM-200 (weighing module) and WTM-500 (indicator) models. The indicators are self-indicating and DC-powered. The instruments are not designed for direct sales to the public. Plastic enclosure; WTM-500 has a 7 segment 0.3\" LED display, 4 operating buttons and 6 enunciator LEDs. Devices: initial zero setting device on power up, semi-automatic zero setting, zero tracking (optional), semi-automatic subtractive tare balancing, zero-indicator, indication of stable equilibrium, net indicator, gravity compensation, printing. Interfaces: load cell connection (6-wire), RS232/485, analogue output, external I/O, Ethernet, Profibus. Software is held in firmware with identification number V1.xx; download of software is prevented by a jumper (JP1) on the main board; access to legally relevant parameters is only allowed via a jumper on the circuit board. Sealing: access to the setup/configuration jumper is prevented by sealing the enclosure via a tamper-evident solution; the load cell connection is sealed via a tamper-evident solution."
